    "body": "Fixes #8149.\n\n`EarlyReplaceBuiltinCalls._optimise_min_max()` put only the arguments after the first into temps, and their evaluation wrapped the whole comparison chain, so `max(f(1), f(2))` called `f(2)` before `f(1)`. All arguments now go into temps and are evaluated from left to right. The first one's temp is reused for the first comparison, so no temp is added, and the generated C for `max(a, b)` only changes the order of the assignments.\n\nNew tests in `tests/run/builtin_min_max.pyx` cover `max` with three calls, `min` of a list literal and `max` of two `cdef int` calls. They fail without the change.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
